      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.18,
          "end": 4.55,
          "en": "When it comes to building layouts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.55,
          "end": 8.97,
          "en": "in React Native apps, Flexbox is super important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.97,
          "end": 12.83,
          "en": "And you might know Flexbox from the web and CSS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.83,
          "end": 15.6,
          "en": "And then the next lecture, will have a little deep dive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.6,
          "end": 17.593,
          "en": "into Flexbox and how to use it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.6,
          "end": 23.09,
          "en": "But Flexbox is a key approach, a key concept",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 23.09,
          "end": 26.73,
          "en": "which is basically a collection of CSS properties",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 26.73,
          "end": 30.88,
          "en": "that you use to control how things look like.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 30.88,
          "end": 34.78,
          "en": "And the Flexbox implemented here in React Native,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 34.78,
          "end": 38.33,
          "en": "which can be set with all those React Native properties,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 38.33,
          "end": 43.33,
          "en": "is very similar to what you know from CSS Flexbox.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 43.49,
          "end": 48.05,
          "en": "In the end Flexbox is all about a couple of CSS properties,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 48.05,
          "end": 51.7,
          "en": "or a couple of styling properties to be precise here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 51.7,
          "end": 55.733,
          "en": "that are about positioning elements inside of containers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 56.67,
          "end": 60.16,
          "en": "You can control how much space certain elements take up,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 60.16,
          "end": 62.4,
          "en": "and if they are to the left or right,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 62.4,
          "end": 65.61,
          "en": "or bottom or top of other elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 65.61,
          "end": 67.74,
          "en": "And the positioning is then controlled",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 67.74,
          "end": 71.34,
          "en": "with the style settings that you apply to the container",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 71.34,
          "end": 75.22,
          "en": "that holds other elements, as you will see in a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 75.22,
          "end": 79.22,
          "en": "Now Flexbox is all about Q-axis",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 79.22,
          "end": 81.31,
          "en": "which you have on a container.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 81.31,
          "end": 83.9,
          "en": "For example, the styles which you see here at the top,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 83.9,
          "end": 87.21000000000001,
          "en": "flex one, flex-direction: column, and so on,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 87.21000000000001,
          "end": 89.46000000000001,
          "en": "would be applied to the container",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 89.46000000000001,
          "end": 91.963,
          "en": "that holds the three boxes inside of it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 93.13,
          "end": 96.33,
          "en": "Now the flex one instruction here, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 96.33,
          "end": 98.85,
          "en": "would tell the container that it should expand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 98.85,
          "end": 103.21000000000001,
          "en": "to occupy all available space, though as you will see soon,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 103.21000000000001,
          "end": 106.1,
          "en": "this is seen in relation to other containers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 106.1,
          "end": 108.27000000000001,
          "en": "that might also take up space.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 108.27000000000001,
          "end": 110.77000000000001,
          "en": "And then flex-direction controls whether the elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 110.77000000000001,
          "end": 114.3,
          "en": "are laid out in a column as you see it here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 114.3,
          "end": 117.95,
          "en": "or in a row as you see it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 117.95,
          "end": 119.663,
          "en": "So that all works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 120.56,
          "end": 123.88,
          "en": "Basically, flex-direction controls if the main axis,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 123.88,
          "end": 128.1,
          "en": "as it's called, is top to bottom or left to right.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 128.1,
          "end": 130.7,
          "en": "With column, it's top to bottom,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 130.7,
          "end": 133.163,
          "en": "with row, it's left to right.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 134.49,
          "end": 137.63,
          "en": "And then you also got other properties like justify-content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 137.63,
          "end": 140.71,
          "en": "or align items that allow you to control",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 140.71,
          "end": 143.95,
          "en": "how the elements are laid out in their axis.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 143.95,
          "end": 145.9,
          "en": "So if there is some space between them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 145.9,
          "end": 148.773,
          "en": "if there are crunched together and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
